text:
maya: FYI I'm seeing a strange edge in the JS SDK sample app when using jsonMode + function/tool calling. If the call triggers an auth refresh (401 -> refresh token -> retry) the jsonMode helper sometimes returns an empty parsed object even though the retried response has valid JSON. Repro below.

ash: Which SDK version and can you paste a tiny repro? :thinking_face:

maya: repro (JS, sdk@0.24.0):
```js
const client = new RedwoodSDK({ jsonMode: true });
const resp = await client.callFunction('cart.get', { cartId: 'u-42' }, {
  schema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {
      products: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { sku: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['sku'] } }
    },
    required: ['products']
  }
});
// If the access token expired: first attempt -> 401, SDK refreshes token and retries.
// Expect: resp.parsed.products = [{ sku: 'T-1000' }]
// Seen: resp.parsed === {}  // parsed object empty
```

sam: Can you log the final response text around the retry path? If the raw body contains the JSON then the bug is in the parse guard.

maya: I added a console.log in the retry handler. The retried response body contains the correct JSON payload. The parser seems to short-circuit when a previous attempt set an auth-error flag.

lia: That matches a Python bug we fixed earlier. We had an internal `hadAuthError` flag that prevented parse from running on the success path after a retry. Workaround: disable jsonMode in the sample or do manual JSON.parse(resp.rawBody) after the call. Not great for onboarding.

ash: I'll take this on. Quick idea: clear transient error flags before the final parse step in the HTTP client retry loop instead of deep in the parser. Also add a unit test that simulates 401 -> refresh -> 200 with jsonMode + schema validate.

sam: Note streaming responses could be impacted too if the guard bypasses the stream consumer and drops buffered chunks. Add an integration test that simulates chunked JSON across retry.

devex-bot: Issue created: github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-js/issues/1319 — "JS SDK: jsonMode parse skipped after auth refresh during function call" by maya. Labels: devex, bug, needs-triage.

maya: Thanks — I'll update the sample-app README with the temporary workaround and link to the issue to avoid onboarding friction. :thumbsup:

ash: For the patch, prefer resetting parse state in the common retry layer to avoid duplicated state in multiple parsers. Also add a regression test for the sample-app's smoke tests.

lia: Pushed a unit test snippet to the issue for parity across JS/Py.

maya: Appreciated. I'll follow the PR and revert the README note once the fix lands.
